    "body": "## Chat05A BLOCKED_ENV recovery: repository-native GitHub-only execution is allowed (2026-10-30)\n\n**Verified remotely:** exact PR #460 branch ref `refs/heads/codex/chat05a-vote-trigger-idempotency-20261030` exists at `463d75ae9181fae886ae9e198698219f95106993`; current `main@b435e70eb88b87b3c3324ef2a2da14cdf473f229`. GitHub connector can read the current branch, PR, source files and Git objects. The last three PR workflows completed successfully. `.github/workflows/chat03b2-private-api.yml` runs `node --test` and a real **isolated GitHub-hosted local workerd/D1** integration test through `gameplay-server/test/private_api_local_test.mjs`. These old checks are **not** tests of future authored-text changes.\n\n**Root cause:** Codex's local checkout is dirty/stale and its process cannot resolve `github.com`. This is a local networking / local Git-object availability failure, not a missing remote PR branch or an implementation blocker. Do not modify or clean its unrelated `.codex/config.toml`.\n\n**Repository policy is explicit:** root `AGENTS.md` says \"GitHub-only workflow\" and `AGENTS.override.md` says ordinary work uses an isolated **remote GitHub branch**; **a local worktree is optional**. Therefore do NOT make a successful local clone/worktree a mandatory gate if the GitHub connector can create atomic commits and GitHub Actions can execute the relevant new tests.\n\n**Permitted recovery for the SAME Chat05A Codex thread / PR #460:**\n1. Re-read canonical Notion, plan, Chat01 and exact [authored-text contract](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/pull/460#issuecomment-6524732970); re-check current branch HEAD, shared-file ownership, policy and CI. Preserve remote HEAD lease; if changed externally, stop and reconcile.\n2. Implement **one minimal complete atom** at a time using GitHub connector on the **existing** branch. For multi-file coherence, upload all changed blobs, construct one tree from the current branch tree, create a single commit with the current HEAD as parent, and fast-forward the existing branch with a **non-force**, exact-`expected_sha` lease. Do not use the default branch and do not create a second branch or PR. Do not issue independent sequential per-file commits for an interdependent security/DB change.\n3. Include executable negative and local Worker/D1 tests with each atom. GitHub Actions' isolated runner is the executable environment; review exact published diff and **check the new HEAD's actual test steps/logs**, not just previous green CI. A connector/API-only write is NOT itself verification. If tests cannot execute reliably in CI, STOP; do not claim PASS.\n4. Atom 1: trusted, versioned ready-phrase snapshot + authenticated, immutable attack/defense text commit; server-origin provenance only; no authored-trigger route yet. Atom 2 after independent verification: coherent lifecycle + source/docs mirrors + D1 migration/invariants + reveal transition, including non-DRAW text edit. Never weaken auth/CAS/uniqueness or existing DRAW and legacy behavior.\n5. For high-risk auth/persistence/shared-lifecycle changes obtain independent `critical_reviewer` against exact published HEAD. If a real independent critical review mechanism is unavailable, STOP and report that gap; do not replace it with your own unsupported claim.\n6. Maintain PR as Draft, no merge, main write, deploy, Cloudflare, secrets, real invitations, Chat05B or other stages. Record exact files, HEAD, CI run links, review and any concrete blockers.\n\n**Alternative only if GitHub connector cannot publish atomic trees or CI cannot run:** request a fresh isolated Codex executor with network access to this **same** PR branch; do not reuse the dirty old checkout, do not reset/clean `.codex/config.toml`. No second simultaneous coding lane.\n\nThis resolves the false \"local clone is a universal prerequisite\" gate, **not** the Chat05A implementation itself. Chat05A remains PARTIAL/BLOCKED until authored-trigger atom tests/review PASS.",
